Radiation count (effective number of light species), if the new species takes its particles from the ordinary
neutrinos after they decouple and is slow by recombination (m >> 0.6 eV):
  at nucleosynthesis: 3.046 (no extra load); at recombination: 2.28 (ordinary neutrinos depleted to 0.75)
If instead it is produced before decoupling at population chi: nucleosynthesis 3.046 + chi; recombination 3.046.

Published bounds to compare [from the literature notes]: Planck 2018 N_eff = 2.99 +- 0.17 (standard model);
galaxy lensing 2-sigma upper limits on extra/baryons inside 300 kpc: 0.58 to 2.67; central values 0.09 to 0.92;
richest six clusters hold A = 3.3 to 8.8 eV-equivalent inside r500 depending on corrections;
cluster cores need K >= 8 (strong corrections) to 17 eV (none), for 95% of systems.
